# D10(a) NEGATIVE (decisions.md, ratified 2026-07-06): binding a mutable
# borrow to a local name (`auto r = &b`) is rejected — a place has one
# exclusive writer, and a named `&`-binding would alias a second writable
# path to it for the rest of the scope. The pre-D10 write-through bind is
# retired. Expected: error[E_LocalBorrowBind] at the `&b` initializer.
void main():
    Vector[int] a = [1, 2, 3]
    Vector[int] b = a
    auto r = &b
    r.push(9)
    print(a.len())
    print(b.len())
    print("done")
